                <pb facs="0435" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg337"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Jackson to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-10-23"><hi rendition="#italic">October 23,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1434.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    this morning of your telegram<anchor n="1" xml:id="d410-f1"/> containing the
                    American answer to certain French proposals with regard to the peace
                    negotiations with China, and to inform you that I at once communicated the same
                    to Baron von Richthofen, at the foreign office. * * *</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Jackson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
